course: dictionary
lesson: 11696
title: Attentive: listening and caring
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Attentive means listening or watching carefully, with your mind on what is in front of you. «The attentive class listened to every word the teacher read.» The clue is listened to every word: the class was focused and did not miss anything.
explain: Attentive can also mean kind and helpful, noticing what other people need. «The attentive waiter filled our glasses before we asked.» He noticed our glasses were empty, so he was paying close attention to us. Try swapping in careful or caring: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Look for common phrases: an attentive listener, attentive to, and listen attentively. Attentively is the adverb, telling you how someone does something. Attentiveness is the noun, the quality of being attentive.
fact: Attentive is an adjective: attentive, more attentive, most attentive.
fact: «Attentive» means listening or watching carefully.
fact: «Attentive» can also mean kind and helpful, noticing what other people need.
fact: «Attentively» is the adverb: «She listened attentively to the story.»
fact: «Attentiveness» is the noun: «The teacher praised the class for their attentiveness.»
exercise: «The attentive class stayed quiet and watched the teacher.» What does attentive mean here? | *Listening or watching carefully | Angry and loud | Tired and sleepy | Very far away
exercise: «Mia listened ___ to the story.» Which word fits the gap? | attentive | attentiveness | attention | *attentively
exercise: «The attentive host noticed our cups were empty and filled them.» What does attentive suggest? | Rude and loud | Lazy and bored | Very old | *Kind and helpful, noticing what others need
test: «The nurse was attentive to every patient on the ward.» What does attentive to mean here? | Sleeping nearby | Ignoring them | *Paying close care and notice to them | Afraid of them
test: Which word is the adverb? | attention | attentiveness | attentive | *attentively
exam: Which sentence uses attentive to mean kind and helpful? | *«The attentive waiter brought extra bread before we asked.» | «The attentive pencil was broken in two.» | «The attentive road was long and steep.» | «The attentive sky was grey all day.»
